          "passageTitle": "Command of Evidence - Support — Q11",
          "passage": "The phrase usa-don sonda is a future-oriented\nexpression used by members of the Yupno, an\nIndigenous group in Papua New Guinea, that\ntranslates to \"next week.\" Rafael Núñez and\ncolleagues recorded Yupno speakers explaining\nseveral of these temporal-related words and\nphrases and coded each speaker's manual\ngestures. Previous research has found evidence\nof Spanish speakers referring to the left/right\naxis to describe events in time, and many\nresearchers believe that this tendency to make\ntemporal distinctions along imagined linear axes\nis universal. However, Núñez and colleagues\nclaim that this tendency is not in fact\nubiquitous.",
